**Reused Evidence**
The main reused item that genuinely bears on 7B is the Adani proximity/favoritism context. It is indirect, so I treat it as contextual rather than decisive.

REUSE_JSON: {"evidence_ids":["E0069"],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.9"]}

**New Evidence**
The strongest affirmative evidence is Modi’s own public asset disclosure, which is concrete personal transparency. The strongest adverse evidence is the PM CARES RTI resistance and the Adani-favoritism network allegations, but those are still mostly indirect to Modi personally.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Details of the Assets: Movable and Immovable of Myself, My Spouse, and All Dependents on 31-03-2022","publisher":"Prime Minister of India","publication_date":"2022-08-09","url":"https://www.pmindia.gov.in/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Shri-Narendra-Modi.pdf","claim":"Modi's disclosure for 31-03-2022 reports cash in hand of Rs 35,250, bank balance of Rs 46,555, FDR/MOD of Rs 2,10,33,226, NSC of Rs 9,05,105, life insurance of Rs 1,89,305, four gold rings valued at Rs 1,73,063, gross assets of Rs 2,23,82,504, no shares or personal loans, and no immovable assets.","locator":"Pages 0-3, asset tables and immovable-assets section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary PMO disclosure with exact line items and explicit asset categories.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 annual disclosure as of 31 March 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Strong and direct: self-disclosed by Modi through the PMO; this supports transparency but does not by itself prove broader honesty on all issues.","contrary_evidence":["It is a voluntary self-declaration, so completeness still depends on truthful reporting."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.3","7B.4","7B.8","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Details of the Assets and Liabilities of the Union Council of Ministers (2022-2023) as on 31.03.2023","publisher":"Prime Minister of India","publication_date":"2023-09 (best available)","url":"https://www.pmindia.gov.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Sh.-Narendra-Modi.pdf","claim":"The 31-03-2023 disclosure again lists no immovable property for Modi and reports a gross total asset value of Rs 2,58,96,444, showing continuity in public asset reporting across years.","locator":"Pages 0-3, asset tables and immovable-assets section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary PMO filing with precise line items and a direct year-over-year follow-up to the 2022 disclosure.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Near-period continuity evidence immediately after the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Strong and direct for Modi's own asset disclosure behavior; still limited to the asset dimension of integrity.","contrary_evidence":["As with any self-filed disclosure, the document is not independent proof of completeness."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.3","7B.4","7B.8","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Assets and Liabilities of the Union Council of Ministers (2021-2022) as on 31.03.2022","publisher":"Prime Minister of India","publication_date":"2022-09-07","url":"https://www.pmindia.gov.in/ur/assets-and-liabilities-of-the-union-council-of-ministers-2021-2022-as-on-31-03-2022-3/","claim":"The PMO publicly maintained an annual assets-and-liabilities index that included Shri Narendra Modi's 2021-2022 disclosure entry, making ministerial asset filings directly available on the PM website.","locator":"index lines 66-69 and surrounding list of cabinet declarations","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official repository page maintained by PMO with annual filing access and explicit Modi entry.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct 2022 disclosure repository and publication pathway.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for transparency practice at the PMO level; limited because the page is an index rather than the underlying sworn statement.","contrary_evidence":["A repository index does not validate the truth of the underlying declaration."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Md Iqbal Ansari vs Prime Minister'S Office on 22 August, 2022","publisher":"Indian Kanoon / Central Information Commission decision","publication_date":"2022-08-22","url":"https://indiankanoon.org/doc/197010425/","claim":"The CIC records that PMO replied PM CARES Fund is not a public authority under RTI, and repeated that position for multiple appeals while directing requesters to the PM CARES website.","locator":"paragraphs 77-112","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct quasi-judicial record with dated pleadings and decision text.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct 2022 legal record about PMO/PM CARES transparency during the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the position is taken by the PMO under the Prime Minister's office structure; it is not proof of personal enrichment but is relevant to scrutiny and concealment issues.","contrary_evidence":["The record concerns institutional transparency, not a finding that Modi personally concealed assets or took illicit benefit."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"NITI Aayog Welcomes Suman Bery as NITI Aayog Vice Chairman","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India","publication_date":"2022-05-01","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/Pressreleaseshare.aspx?PRID=1821686&lang=2&reg=48","claim":"The government appointed Suman Bery as NITI Aayog Vice Chairman effective 1 May 2022, describing him as an experienced policy economist and research administrator with prior roles at NCAER, the Prime Minister's Economic Advisory Council, the Statistical Commission, and the RBI's monetary policy advisory apparatus.","locator":"opening paragraphs of the release","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary appointment release with explicit professional background and exact effective date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 personnel action.","ruler_attribution":"Strong: this is a PM-directed senior appointment in a central policy body, though it still does not prove absence of favoritism everywhere else.","contrary_evidence":["Technocratic credentials do not by themselves prove the appointee was fully independent in practice."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"NITI Aayog Welcomes Parameswaran Iyer as Its CEO","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India","publication_date":"2022-07-11","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1840753","claim":"NITI Aayog said Parameswaran Iyer became its CEO on 11 July 2022 and highlighted over 25 years of water-and-sanitation experience, including spearheading the Swachh Bharat Mission and serving as Secretary in the Drinking Water and Sanitation ministry.","locator":"opening paragraphs of the release","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary appointment release with a detailed professional background and exact date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 personnel action.","ruler_attribution":"Strong: PMO-linked senior administrative appointment; positive for professional staffing, though not proof that every appointment was merit-only.","contrary_evidence":["The appointment does not alone demonstrate broader anti-nepotism practice across government."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Circulars and Notifications","publisher":"NITI Aayog","publication_date":"2022-12-01 (best available for the listed notification entry)","url":"https://www.niti.gov.in/disclosures-rti/disclosures/circular-notifications-0","claim":"The NITI Aayog notifications index lists the December 2022 notification regarding appointment of Shri Arvind Virmani as Member, NITI Aayog, and the July 2022 notification of Shri Parameswaran Iyer as CEO.","locator":"table entries 14 and 26","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official notifications index with explicit dated entries for the appointments.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct 2022 administrative record.","ruler_attribution":"Strong at the level of central appointment practice; limited because the index does not itself explain selection criteria or independence in office.","contrary_evidence":["A notification list shows appointment, not why the person was chosen."],"lenses":["7B.5"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Dr Arvind Virmani","publisher":"NITI Aayog","publication_date":"2026-07-20 (accessed; current profile describing 2022 appointment)","url":"https://www.niti.gov.in/about-us/whos-who/leadership/members/dr-arvind-virmani","claim":"NITI Aayog's profile describes Arvind Virmani as a macroeconomist with prior service as Executive Director at the IMF, Chief Economic Advisor in the Ministry of Finance, and Principal Advisor in the Planning Commission, and says he is a Member of NITI Aayog.","locator":"biographical paragraphs on the member profile","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official institutional biography with detailed professional background; current profile but directly relevant to the 2022 appointment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Background evidence for the 2022 appointment period.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for competence of the appointee; limited for Modi personally because biography does not show the selection process or any absence of favoritism by itself.","contrary_evidence":["Professional competence of an appointee does not rule out political selection motives."],"lenses":["7B.5"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Suman Bery, Vice Chairperson, NITI Aayog","publisher":"NITI Aayog","publication_date":"2026-07-20 (accessed; current profile describing 2022 appointment)","url":"https://www.niti.gov.in/node/1462","claim":"NITI Aayog's profile says Suman Bery took over as Vice Chairperson on 1 May 2022 and describes him as an experienced policy economist and research administrator with prior roles at the World Bank, NCAER, the Prime Minister's Economic Advisory Council, the Statistical Commission, and RBI advisory bodies.","locator":"lines 8703-8721","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official institutional profile with explicit appointment date and detailed professional background.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Background evidence for the 2022 appointment period.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for appointee competence; limited because it still does not show appointment criteria or independence beyond the bio.","contrary_evidence":["A competent bio does not by itself establish that the appointment was made without loyalty or patronage considerations."],"lenses":["7B.5"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"NITI Aayog (notifications index)","publisher":"NITI Aayog","publication_date":"2022-12-01 (best available for the listed notification entry)","url":"https://www.niti.gov.in/disclosures-rti/disclosures/circular-notifications-0","claim":"The NITI Aayog circulars page publicly lists the July 2022 appointment notification for Shri Parameswaran Iyer as CEO and the December 2022 appointment notification for Shri Arvind Virmani as Member.","locator":"table entries 26 and 14","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official public index of notifications, directly linking the relevant 2022 appointment entries.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct 2022 administrative record.","ruler_attribution":"Strong at the level of transparency around appointments; limited because the index does not explain appointment criteria or independence.","contrary_evidence":["A public notification list is not evidence that all appointments were merit-based."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.6"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Adani Watch piece on Adani coverage and pressure","publisher":"Reuters Institute for the Study of Journalism","publication_date":"2023-02-07","url":"https://reutersinstitute.politics.ox.ac.uk/news/global-outlets-paid-attention-small-site-had-been-digging-adani-group-years-despite-lawsuits-and-threats","claim":"The article says Gautam Adani is seen by independent observers as a close aide to Prime Minister Narendra Modi and that the Adani Group has received massive government contracts in energy and infrastructure; it also describes lawsuits and other pressure faced by journalists investigating the group.","locator":"paragraphs 206-218","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reputable research-journalism outlet summarizing investigative reporting and observer claims; useful but still inferential on Modi-specific favoritism.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Explains a 2022-anchored patronage/favoritism controversy but is published just after the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate and indirect: the article links the network to Modi through observers' inference, not a direct finding of Modi personal benefit or instruction.","contrary_evidence":["The piece is not a formal finding of corruption and relies partly on outside observers' interpretation."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.7","7B.9"]}

**Search And Rejection Summary**
I reviewed roughly 25-30 documents across PMO asset disclosures, NITI Aayog appointments and biographies, RTI/legal records on PM CARES, Reuters Institute reporting on Adani, Reuters/Reuters-feed reporting on government-business proximity, and several fact-check and opinion-adjacent items that I did not keep.

Kept because they were directly useful:
- PMO asset disclosure PDF for 31-03-2022.
- PMO asset disclosure PDF for 31-03-2023.
- PMO assets-and-liabilities index page for the 2021-2022 filing.
- CIC / Indian Kanoon PM CARES RTI decision from 22 Aug 2022.
- PIB releases for Suman Bery and Parameswaran Iyer appointments.
- NITI Aayog notification index and bios for Virmani and Bery.
- Reuters Institute Adani article for favoritism / pressure context.

Rejected as duplicate, weak, or off-target:
- Repeated asset-report summaries from Indian Express, NDTV, Times of India, and other outlets that restated the same PMO disclosure without adding new facts.
- Fact-checks about other people's misuse of Modi clips or false headlines, because they do not show Modi personally lying or correcting himself.
- Broad country-level corruption or governance indicators, because they are context only and do not establish ruler-specific personal integrity.
- Economic, social, or foreign-policy chapter materials already collected in 5B/6B/2B unless they directly showed a personal-nexus integrity issue. I did not convert those into integrity evidence.

**Remaining Gaps**
- There is still no strong direct 2022 evidence of deliberate falsehood by Modi personally that is independent of broader political rhetoric.
- The clearest adverse material is still indirect: PM CARES transparency resistance and the Adani proximity/favoritism network, neither of which is a clean personal finding against Modi himself.
- I did not find a 2022 court, audit, or sanctions finding showing Modi personally benefited from office through hidden assets, bribes, or direct self-dealing.
- If you want a tighter 7B dossier, the most useful next search would be campaign finance / procurement / PM CARES governance / Modi-specific interview correction evidence, but the current record is already enough to support a cautious, mixed-attribution dossier without scoring.
